WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.152 --> 00:00:13.953
Errol seemed flustered when Mr.

2
00:00:13.973 --> 00:00:15.714
Havisham and Cedric arrived.

3
00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.435
"I'm sorry, Mr.

4
00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:21.216
Havisham," she said, "but I must speak to my servant.

5
00:00:22.597 --> 00:00:25.038
Mary has just received some terrible news."

6
00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:29.880
Mrs. Errol hurried into the kitchen, leaving Cedric to entertain the lawyer.

7
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.483
Mr. Havisham sat in a chair while Cedric took a seat opposite him.

8
00:00:38.325 --> 00:00:42.629
Mr. Havisham wasn't used to talking to children and had no idea what to say.

9
00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.552
Cedric finally broke the silence.

10
00:00:46.572 --> 00:00:49.995
"I don't really understand what an earl is.

11
00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:53.878
And when a boy is going to be one, he ought to know."

12
00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.101
Mr. Havisham was relieved.

13
00:00:58.062 --> 00:00:59.844
This was a topic he could talk about.

14
00:01:01.108 --> 00:01:04.529
"Earls are important men," the lawyer began.

15
00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:08.930
"Over the centuries they've helped to govern England.

16
00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:16.972
They usually come from very old families and—" Cedric popped up from the sofa with excitement.

17
00:01:16.992 --> 00:01:20.513
"The woman who sells apples is very old!

18
00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.414
She must be close to a hundred!"

19
00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:30.516
"Well an old person is not the same as an old family.

20
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:37.303
The first Earl of Dorincourt received his title almost four hundred years ago."

21
00:01:37.323 --> 00:01:41.104
"Oh, I see."

22
00:01:42.405 --> 00:01:43.445
Cedric sat down.

23
00:01:44.866 --> 00:01:46.527
They fell into silence again.

24
00:01:48.748 --> 00:01:51.049
Mr. Havisham studied a crack in the wall.

25
00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:54.970
Cedric sighed.

26
00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.432
"Sometimes I wish I had lots of money."

27
00:02:00.264 --> 00:02:02.386
Mr. Havisham raised his eyebrows.

28
00:02:02.406 --> 00:02:04.427
"What would you do with it?"

29
00:02:04.447 --> 00:02:11.732
"I'd buy the apple seller a tent for her stall and a stove and a warm shawl.

30
00:02:13.113 --> 00:02:17.276
She's so poor that she has to work every day, even when it's raining."

31
00:02:18.777 --> 00:02:20.157
Cedric stopped to think.

32
00:02:20.178 --> 00:02:25.261
"And on rainy days, I'd give her a dollar so she could stay home!"

33
00:02:26.982 --> 00:02:29.524
Mr. Havisham smiled at his generosity.

34
00:02:30.308 --> 00:02:32.330
"Why would you do all that?"

35
00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:36.593
"Because she's been kind to me," Cedric explained.

36
00:02:36.613 --> 00:02:41.576
"When I fell and cut my knee, she gave me an apple for free."

37
00:02:45.239 --> 00:02:46.900
was kind," Mr.

38
00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.001
Havisham agreed.

39
00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:52.284
He suddenly found himself enjoying this conversation.

40
00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:54.365
"What else would you do?"

41
00:02:54.385 --> 00:02:57.568
"I'd like to help my friend Dick.

42
00:02:58.624 --> 00:03:03.426
He's just a few years older than I am, but he has a shoeshine stand with a partner.

43
00:03:04.787 --> 00:03:07.728
Once I had a new ball that bounced into the street.

44
00:03:09.268 --> 00:03:11.349
Dick ran after it and brought it back.

45
00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:13.850
We've been friends ever since."

46
00:03:16.331 --> 00:03:17.312
Cedric frowned.

47
00:03:17.332 --> 00:03:20.453
"The shoeshine business isn't too good right now."

48
00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:26.916
Mr. Havisham forced himself not to smile at Cedric's knowledge of the shoeshine business.

49
00:03:28.016 --> 00:03:29.516
"And why is that?"

50
00:03:29.536 --> 00:03:35.758
"Well, everybody likes Dick, but nobody likes his partner.

51
00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:38.659
Jake's a bad guy.

52
00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.480
I wish Dick could have his own shoeshine stand."

53
00:03:45.401 --> 00:03:47.161
Mr. Havisham leaned forward.

54
00:03:47.181 --> 00:03:48.922
"What about you?

55
00:03:49.582 --> 00:03:51.103
Is there anything you want?"

56
00:03:53.123 --> 00:03:54.083
Cedric grinned.

57
00:03:54.103 --> 00:03:55.824
"A pony!

58
00:03:56.516 --> 00:04:00.038
Sometimes when Mama and I are walking, we see a boy riding.

59
00:04:01.178 --> 00:04:02.299
I'd like to ride!"

60
00:04:03.659 --> 00:04:04.560
Just then Mrs.

61
00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.921
Errol came into the parlor, looking upset.

62
00:04:06.941 --> 00:04:11.523
"Mary's husband is sick, and now he's lost his job."

63
00:04:11.543 --> 00:04:14.164
"I must talk to her!"

64
00:04:15.264 --> 00:04:17.866
Cedric slipped from the sofa and left the room.

65
00:04:17.886 --> 00:04:21.507
"That's quite a boy you have," Mr.

66
00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:22.768
Havisham said to Mrs.

67
00:04:22.888 --> 00:04:27.286
Errol. "There will be many changes in his life.

68
00:04:28.426 --> 00:04:34.369
One day he'll have lots of power—" "Oh, he's just a little boy!

69
00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:37.631
I hope I can teach him to use his power wisely."

70
00:04:38.532 --> 00:04:40.433
Mrs. Errol seemed distressed.

71
00:04:40.453 --> 00:04:45.435
"Cedric will have lots of money too," Mr.

72
00:04:45.455 --> 00:04:46.616
Havisham went on.

73
00:04:46.636 --> 00:04:50.398
"The earl wants me to buy whatever he wants.

74
00:04:51.138 --> 00:04:53.880
But Cedric only wants to help others.

75
00:04:55.132 --> 00:04:58.094
I don't think that's what the earl had in mind."

76
00:05:00.856 --> 00:05:02.998
Mrs. Errol gave a sympathetic sigh.

77
00:05:03.018 --> 00:05:05.820
"That poor, lonely man.

78
00:05:07.281 --> 00:05:11.203
His sons have died, and now he just wants to be kind to my boy."

79
00:05:11.223 --> 00:05:15.386
Mr. Havisham couldn't look her in the eye.

80
00:05:16.247 --> 00:05:18.809
The earl was far different from what she imagined.

81
00:05:20.009 --> 00:05:23.332
The earl's motive was to ensure that Cedric would come to England.

82
00:05:24.448 --> 00:05:29.090
"Give my grandson whatever he wants," the earl had told Mr.

83
00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:32.872
Havisham. "I don't care what you spend.

84
00:05:33.732 --> 00:05:37.554
Make sure he has money in his pocket and knows it came from me."

85
00:05:41.595 --> 00:05:43.916
Cedric walked slowly back into the parlor.

86
00:05:45.037 --> 00:05:49.018
"Mary doesn't know how they'll pay the rent," he said sadly.

87
00:05:49.038 --> 00:05:52.480
"Their landlord is threatening to evict them.

88
00:05:53.848 --> 00:05:55.229
I wish we could help them."

89
00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:58.912
Mr. Havisham made a quick decision.

90
00:05:59.772 --> 00:06:02.774
He reached into his pocket and handed some money to Cedric.

91
00:06:04.195 --> 00:06:07.517
"I'm sure the earl would want Mary to have this."

92
00:06:09.218 --> 00:06:11.240
"Twenty-five dollars!"

93
00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:14.862
Cedric's eyes widened in amazement.

94
00:06:14.882 --> 00:06:17.844
"That's a fortune!"

95
00:06:18.284 --> 00:06:19.345
Mrs. Errol said.

96
00:06:20.866 --> 00:06:24.541
Running toward the kitchen, Cedric called out, "Mary!

97
00:06:24.921 --> 00:06:27.542
Look what I have for you from my grandfather!"

98
00:06:29.684 --> 00:06:33.206
He returned a few minutes later, a big smile on his face.

99
00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:39.409
"I never saw anybody cry with joy like Mary just did," Cedric said.

100
00:06:39.429 --> 00:06:43.572
"Maybe being an earl won't be so bad after all!"
